---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Koozy — Simple, Fast Live Multiplayer Quizzes"
  description="Learn why we built Koozy: live multiplayer quizzes without projectors, app downloads, or paywalls. Simple for hosts, fun for players."
  noindex={false}
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-10 md:py-16">
    <div class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-16">
      <div class="inline-block text-xs uppercase font-extrabold tracking-widest text-[#6c4de8] mb-3 bg-[#eeeafd] px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-[#c9bfff]">
        Our Mission
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-[#191817] tracking-tight leading-tight mb-4">
        Making Learning <span class="font-hand text-[#6c4de8] font-normal">Fun & Social.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base text-[#77736c] leading-relaxed">
        Live quizzes are one of the best ways to learn, retain knowledge, and bring groups together.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- The Problem We Saw -->
    <section class="kz-card-tactile p-6 sm:p-8 bg-white mb-12">
      <div class="font-hand text-2xl text-[#6c4de8] -rotate-2 select-none mb-1">
        why we started ✦
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-[#191817] mb-4">
        Live quizzes should not require two screens.
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#77736c] leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          For years, live quiz games required an awkward setup: questions were projected on a big screen, while players tapped plain color blocks on their phones. In remote meetings or classrooms without a projector, playing together was frustrating.
        </p>
        <p>
          On top of that, corporate paywalls, player caps, and constant app download prompts got in the way of having fun.
        </p>
        <p>
          We built <strong class="text-[#191817]">Koozy</strong> to change that: questions appear directly on every player's device, joining takes 5 seconds with a PIN, and anyone can host for free.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Three Pillars -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-[#191817] mb-8 text-center">
        The Principles Behind Koozy
      </h2>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="kz-card-tactile p-6 bg-[#fffdf7]">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-[#e6f9ff] text-[#05cdff] font-mono font-bold flex items-center justify-center border-2 border-[#191817] mb-3">
            01
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-black text-[#191817] mb-2">Zero Friction</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-[#77736c] leading-relaxed">
            Players should never be forced to install an app or create an account to play a 5-minute quiz. A 5-letter PIN and a nickname is all anyone needs.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="kz-card-tactile p-6 bg-[#fffdf7]">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-[#eeeafd] text-[#6c4de8] font-mono font-bold flex items-center justify-center border-2 border-[#191817] mb-3">
            02
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-black text-[#191817] mb-2">Device-Native UI</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-[#77736c] leading-relaxed">
            Questions, options, and timers live directly on the device you are holding. Play in person, over a Discord voice chat, or across continents seamlessly.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="kz-card-tactile p-6 bg-[#fffdf7]">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-[#e6ffe6] text-[#00cc05] font-mono font-bold flex items-center justify-center border-2 border-[#191817] mb-3">
            03
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-black text-[#191817] mb-2">Tactile Delight</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-[#77736c] leading-relaxed">
            We reject sterile, boring corporate SaaS design. Koozy embraces hand-drawn accents, bold tactile buttons, and playful micro-interactions that make learning feel like a game.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Architecture & Technology -->
    <section class="kz-card-tactile p-6 sm:p-8 bg-white mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-[#191817] mb-4">
        Modern Real-Time Architecture
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#77736c] leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Behind Koozy's playful exterior is an asynchronous real-time engine:
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs">
        <div class="p-4 bg-[#f7f5ef] rounded-xl border border-[#d8d3ca]">
          <strong class="text-[#191817] block mb-1 font-bold">Django Channels & Daphne</strong>
          Asynchronous WebSocket brokers managing real-time lobby state, timer synchronization, and live answer broadcasts.
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-[#f7f5ef] rounded-xl border border-[#d8d3ca]">
          <strong class="text-[#191817] block mb-1 font-bold">Google Gemini AI</strong>
          Integrated generation pipeline producing balanced 4-option MCQs with strict validation schemas.
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-[#f7f5ef] rounded-xl border border-[#d8d3ca]">
          <strong class="text-[#191817] block mb-1 font-bold">Astro 5 & React 19</strong>
          Zero-JS static delivery for public presentation, paired with interactive React islands for live multiplayer sessions.
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-[#f7f5ef] rounded-xl border border-[#d8d3ca]">
          <strong class="text-[#191817] block mb-1 font-bold">Google OAuth 2.0</strong>
          Frictionless, secure host authentication without passwords to manage.
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
